<%- include('partials/header') %>

<!-- Mission Hero -->
<section class="mission-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="badge badge-orange">Our Core Belief</span>
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 44px; margin-top: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Protecting Every Dog From the Summer Heat</h1>
    <p>
      At Dogfriz, we are dedicated to saving lives through a combination of precision thermal engineering and science-backed canine hot-weather education.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Content Section -->
<section class="home-section" style="padding-top: 40px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="mission-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="badge badge-blue">Why We Started</span>
        <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 32px; margin-top: 12px; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Canine Cooling Crisis</h2>
        <p style="color: var(--slate-gray); margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 16px;">
          Humans are highly efficient cooling machines. We possess millions of sweat glands spread across almost our entire body. But our dogs are very different. They have sweat glands only on their tiny paw pads, and rely almost 100% on **panting** to shed body heat.
        </p>
        <p style="color: var(--slate-gray); font-size: 16px;">
          When temperatures exceed 90°F, or when humidity makes panting ineffective, a dog's normal body temperature (101°F) can skyrocket to critical heatstroke levels (106°F+) in under 15 minutes. We saw a gap in the market: most "dog gear" was either aesthetic-only or functionally flawed. We set out to fix that by merging canine biology with material science.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <div style="background-color: var(--ice-blue-bg); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 40px; border: 1px solid rgba(0, 153, 184, 0.1);">
        <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-serif); margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 24px;">The Three Tenets of Summer Safety</h3>
        <ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0;">
          <li style="margin-bottom: 24px; display: flex; gap: 16px;">
            <span style="font-size: 28px;">🦺</span>
            <div>
              <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 4px;">1. External Thermal Deflection</strong>
              <span style="color: var(--slate-gray); font-size: 14px;">Blocking direct solar radiation from reaching the dog's skin while using evaporative mesh to simulate cooling sweat.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 24px; display: flex; gap: 16px;">
            <span style="font-size: 28px;">🍼</span>
            <div>
              <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 4px;">2. Proactive Hydration</strong>
              <span style="color: var(--slate-gray); font-size: 14px;">Offering small, frequent sips of cool, clean water to directly reduce oral and respiratory thermal buildup.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 0; display: flex; gap: 16px;">
            <span style="font-size: 28px;">🧠</span>
            <div>
              <strong style="display: block; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 4px;">3. Scientific Awareness</strong>
              <span style="color: var(--slate-gray); font-size: 14px;">Educating parents to check pavement temperatures, recognize breathing restrictions, and administer first aid.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
